  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.89,
      "end_seconds": 5.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Hmm, morning, doctor. Lovely to to meet you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.41,
      "end_seconds": 12.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.78,
      "end_seconds": 18.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "um so... a chesty cough that's why I came"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.8,
      "end_seconds": 23.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "how long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.79,
      "end_seconds": 28.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Ever since... since last Tuesday really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.31,
      "end_seconds": 35.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.53,
      "end_seconds": 60.7,
      "duration_seconds": 24.17,
      "text": "Maybe a five out of ten on a bad day. It happens every other day. Warm drinks helps a bit. I've had a sore chest from coughing too for two weeks. About sore chest from coughing I'd say severe. It's a couple of times a week. I've been feeling feverish too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.36,
      "end_seconds": 65.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.96,
      "end_seconds": 68.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "No surgery, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.48,
      "end_seconds": 83.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "Okay, has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.64,
      "end_seconds": 89.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Yes, naproxen, it gives me a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.29,
      "end_seconds": 108.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "alright, do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.83,
      "end_seconds": 114.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Tiotropium inhaler. I take it it once a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.92,
      "end_seconds": 120.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "okay, any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.48,
      "end_seconds": 124.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "I have COPD for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.77,
      "end_seconds": 130.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.26,
      "end_seconds": 138.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.86,
      "end_seconds": 142.71,
      "duration_seconds": 0.85,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.13,
      "end_seconds": 148.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "I smoke roughly a pack every two days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.79,
      "end_seconds": 149.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.0,
      "end_seconds": 154.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.63,
      "end_seconds": 163.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "so do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.2,
      "end_seconds": 170.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.72,
      "end_seconds": 174.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.02,
      "end_seconds": 178.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.66,
      "end_seconds": 184.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.92,
      "end_seconds": 188.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "My father had bowel cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.42,
      "end_seconds": 194.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Did you get leg swelling or sharp chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.18,
      "end_seconds": 201.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "no leg swelling or sharp chest pain, none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.8,
      "end_seconds": 204.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "yes. Any night sweats or ankle swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.3,
      "end_seconds": 210.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.49,
      "end_seconds": 213.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.41,
      "end_seconds": 217.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "no skin's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.68,
      "end_seconds": 221.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.82,
      "end_seconds": 237.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "nearly done with the readings.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.83,
      "end_seconds": 263.61,
      "duration_seconds": 12.78,
      "text": "okay: height 186 centimetres temperature is 37.1 degrees pressure 142 over 90 weight 59 kilos saturation 92 percent respiratory rate 23 heart rate 101 BMI works out to 17.1."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.77,
      "end_seconds": 270.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.78,
      "end_seconds": 274.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.1,
      "end_seconds": 294.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "there are scattered wheezes on both sides and and no crackles"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.04,
      "end_seconds": 302.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "You can sit up now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.72,
      "end_seconds": 324.4,
      "duration_seconds": 9.68,
      "text": "right, here's what I'm thinking i can't pin this down yet we're looking at an infective exacerbation of chronic lung disease or a pneumonia"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.9,
      "end_seconds": 327.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.82,
      "end_seconds": 342.28,
      "duration_seconds": 14.46,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like an infective exacerbation of chronic lung disease but I'd like to confirm. I think a sputum sample makes sense here for purulent sputum."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 343.84,
      "end_seconds": 346.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "The earliest is Friday, 2 pm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 348.05,
      "end_seconds": 350.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Friday, that works for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.22,
      "end_seconds": 380.5,
      "duration_seconds": 28.28,
      "text": "We'll begin with doxycycline, 100 milligrams, twice a day, for five days. You take it by mouth. That That should help with chest infection. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. We'll begin with prednisolone, 30 milligrams, once a day, for five days. It's for flare of lung disease. If you smoke, this is a good moment to stop, and we can help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 381.0,
      "end_seconds": 385.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "Do I need a chest X-ray? I read it might help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.67,
      "end_seconds": 409.26,
      "duration_seconds": 21.59,
      "text": "I wouldn't order it today. If anything changes, we'll reconsider. Please don't wait if you become more breathless or your lips turn blue. That's when to be seen urgently. Book a review in two weeks. Alright, can you tell me the plan back in your own words, so I know I've explained it clearly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 410.94,
      "end_seconds": 422.3,
      "duration_seconds": 11.36,
      "text": "So, I take the doxycycline, 100 milligrams, twice a day and take the prednisolone, 30 milligrams, once a day. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 423.59,
      "end_seconds": 428.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Yes exactly right. Alright that's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 429.42,
      "end_seconds": 432.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "No, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}